<title>FRANCE: French employers see 97 welfare gap near 40 bln Ff.</title>
<headline>French employers see 97 welfare gap near 40 bln Ff.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jean Gandois, chairman of France's employers' federation CNPF, predicted on Sunday a 1997 welfare deficit of nearly 40 billion francs.</p>
<p>&quot;I expect that the social security deficit for 1997 will be near 40 billion francs, probably slightly below 40 billion francs,&quot; Gandois told RTL radio.</p>
<p>In April France's social security accounts body ACOSS put the welfare deficit for 1997 at 35 billion francs.</p>
<p>The social security system is funded mainly from payroll taxes and covers heathcare, pensions and family benefits.</p>
<p>((-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432))</p>
